@title Famicom Mini - Xevious (Japan)
@file Famicom Mini - Vol. 07 - Xevious (J).gba
@game FXVJ
@chip EEPROM 4Kbit
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba

# Title, 1 PLAYER, area 1 firing zapper and blaster together for 40 taps,
# the L+R menu (the first DOWN after the checkpoint is not taken, hence four)
# > ハイスコアをセーブする: "ハイスコアをセーブしました", A back to the game.
# The save is 17 bytes of the 4 Kbit EEPROM. The score never passes the
# default 20000, so [load] shows the same HI-SCORE: title, 1 PLAYER, area 1.
# From f611 (area 1's first frames) the second reference plays another
# game: other Toroid waves, another explosion behind the menus. It ran a
# frame ahead of dingbat-bios and mgba through the boot (f61 on; its boot
# lead, docs/playtest-bugs.md §65), so START (f361) reached the NES program
# on another of its frames. dingbat-bios and mgba hash alike on every frame
# to f1200.
# Audio (every dingbat configuration, against both references): clicks in
# the silences (title f15, f150, f217, f284, f352; menus f1227-f1631). The
# game plays through FIFO A only (timer 0, 32768 Hz), from three 160-byte
# buffers at 0x03005D40/5DE0/5E80 that its timer 1 interrupt hands DMA 1 in
# turn; they hold 00 in silence. Each click is the four bytes B9 23 00 08
# (dingbat's output -284, 140, 0, 32: the bytes times four), the word at
# 0x03005F20 just past the third buffer, the low half of a pointer
# 0x080023B9. So about every 67 frames dingbat's FIFO DMA fetches one word
# past the buffer before the interrupt restarts it; mgba never does. A
# DMA-request against interrupt-latency race in dingbat, not traced further.
# The second reference is not told this cartridge's 4 Kbit EEPROM size
# (FXVJ is not in emu.py's EEPROM_4K): it writes 8 KB.

[new]
wait 300
checkpoint title window=30
press START
wait 240
checkpoint stage_start window=30
tap A+B times=40 every=12 hold=4
checkpoint gameplay window=30
press L+R hold=10
wait 60
checkpoint menu window=30
press DOWN
wait 20
press DOWN
wait 20
press DOWN
wait 20
press DOWN
wait 20
checkpoint menu_save window=30
press A
wait 60
wait 120
checkpoint saved window=30
press A
wait 120
[load]
wait 300
checkpoint continue_title window=30
press START
wait 240
checkpoint stage_start window=30
tap A times=20 every=12 hold=4
checkpoint gameplay window=30
